Alternative icon sets ("skins") for the Xymon web pages.

Each directory here is a complete skin: every status icon in the
"gifs" directory (<colour>, <colour>-recent, <colour>-ack, unknown,
unknown-recent), the icons of the info, trends and client columns,
the event-log arrow and the graph zoom icon, as SVG.
The page backgrounds, the favicons and xymonbody.css are links to
the files in "gifs", so a skin only replaces the icons.

To use one, run "xymonsettings.sh skin accessible" (or vector, or
classic for the icons in "gifs"), which sets these in xymonserver.cfg;
see xymonsettings(8):

	XYMONSKIN="$XYMONSERVERWWWURL/skins/accessible"
	IMAGEFILETYPE="svg"
	INFOCOLUMNGIF="info.svg"
	TRENDSCOLUMNGIF="trends.svg"
	CLIENTCOLUMNGIF="clientlog.svg"

The last three name the image of the info, trends and client columns
with its extension, so IMAGEFILETYPE does not change them.

Then wait for the next xymongen run. The status pages from the CGIs
change at once. See xymonserver.cfg(5) for both settings.

accessible: every colour has its own shape as well as its own
    colour (circle, triangle, octagon, diamond, square, dashed
    circle), and the colours are the Okabe-Ito palette, so a status
    can be told apart without colour vision. A recent change is a
    filled icon; an acknowledged one is grey with a white check.
vector: flat icons, a different symbol for each colour. A recent
    change is a filled circle with a face; an acknowledged one is a
    check mark in the status colour.

In both sets, the icons that move in "gifs" move too -- red, yellow,
purple and the recent red, yellow, purple and blue -- with a CSS
animation in the SVG, which stops when the browser is set to reduce
motion.

index.txt lists the sets here, for the Look and feel page, which previews
them; add the name of a set you install.

For pages that should not move at all, every set has a "static"
directory with the same icons standing still: point XYMONSKIN at
"$XYMONSERVERWWWURL/skins/accessible/static", for instance, or at
"$XYMONSERVERWWWURL/gifs/static" for the default icons, or run
"xymonsettings.sh animation off". Everything in it that does not move
is a link to the file one level up.

